03Cbr\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EWhich colours and fabrics work best depending on the occasion?\u003C/strong\u003E \u003Cbr\u003EClassic tones (black, navy, grey, beige) are ideal for everyday wear and events. If you want a standout look, opt for brighter colours. In terms of fabric, wool blends add structure and warmth, while lighter finishes and textured materials can elevate the outfit without feeling heavy.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EHow do you choose the right size for a comfortable suit fit?\u003Cbr\u003E\u003C/strong\u003E Make sure the blazer sits well on the shoulders and can be fastened without pulling. With trousers, look for stability at the waist and comfort when sitting. If you want an oversized look, consider sizing up in the blazer; if you prefer a sharper fit, stick to your usual size.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EIs it better to buy the full suit set or build it with separates? \u003Cbr\u003E\u003C/strong\u003EA full set is the quickest option for formal outfits and guarantees a coordinated finish. Buying separates gives you more combinations: a neutral blazer can work with multiple trousers, and tailored trousers instantly elevate shirts, tops and knitwear. For maximum versatility, start with a core duo (double-breasted blazer + straight-leg trousers) and add one trend piece (wide-leg or pinstripe).\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E",
